{
 "what": "The material library (L1 B2): every lit surface's cel class, the only place a class's numbers live. cel: the per-material uniforms of shaders/cel.gdshaderinc (band, mid, form, spec, nmap, ink, rim_k; see its header); sheen: a metal's second, sky-colored band (rule 6) where a shader carries it; edge: the crowd's own rim (width in 1-n.v, step). paint: B3's painted-block parameters, the colors measured from the boards by tools/style/board_measure.py (boxes in board pixels with optional Oklab masks; re-run it to re-measure): paint.lit as painted on the board (lit paint), paint.albedo the same with the board's light divided out (lights; B2r2). B3 paints from albedo. shaders: each adopting shader's default class (its CEL_* defines must equal it: godot/tests/MaterialLibraryTests.cs). assign: material to class, first match wins (shader path, material name and asset path as .NET regexes; all given must match). exclude: what is not converted, by design.",
